<title>USA: Ashworth gets extended $20 mln credit line.</title>
<headline>Ashworth gets extended $20 mln credit line.</headline>
<dateline>CARLSBAD, Calif. 1996-12-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ashworth Inc said Thursday that it has a new, two-year $20 million line of credit with Bank of America to be used for general corporate purposes.</p>
<p>Ashworth said the new agreement expires March 1, 1999, and increases the credit limit from a previous limit of $17 million.</p>
<p>The retailer of gold sportswear said it has borrowings of $50,000 on its line of credit, compared to $8.4 million in borrowings at this time last year.</p>
